     19. The method defined in  claim 16 , the beam steering element being capable of motion in a first direction in response to a first drive signal and also being capable of motion in a second direction independent of the first direction in response to a second drive signal, wherein determining the second control signal comprises determining the first and second drive signals for the beam steering element, and wherein modulating the second control signal by the precession signal comprises modulating the first drive signal by a first component precession signal and modulating the second drive signal by second component precession signal. 


     20. The method defined in  claim 19 , wherein the first component precession signal and the second component precession signal are periodic with a common frequency and are in phase quadrature. 


     21. The method defined in  claim 20 , wherein the trajectory described by the deflected optical beam is a circular orbit with a frequency corresponding to the common frequency. 


