    a fluid outlet defined by the housing and configured to discharge filtered fluid from the filtration chamber; and
    an ejection mechanism operably coupled to the housing and configured to selectively displace the filter element from the filtration chamber.

A method for gain measurement and monitoring in a wireless communication system, comprising:
receiving an input signal at an amplifier within the wireless communication system;
measuring a first characteristic of the input signal;
amplifying the input signal to produce an output signal;
measuring a second characteristic of the output signal;
determining an operational gain value based on the measured first characteristic and the measured second characteristic; and
monitoring said operational gain value by comparing said operational gain value to a predetermined gain threshold.

A low profile spinal prosthesis comprising:
