    a readout circuit coupled to the charge transfer mechanism, the readout circuit configured to convert the transferred electrical charge into an output signal; and
    an output terminal coupled to the readout circuit, the output terminal configured to output the output signal.

An apparatus for controlled removal of stenotic material from a stent located within a body lumen, comprising:
a flexible catheter body configured for intravascular delivery to a stent deployed within a body lumen;
a treatment element disposed at a distal end of the flexible catheter body, the treatment element configured to interact with and remove stenotic material from the stent;
a sensing element disposed at the distal end of the flexible catheter body, the sensing element configured to detect a characteristic difference between the stenotic material and the stent material;
a control unit operably coupled to the flexible catheter body, the control unit configured to receive data from the sensing element and to regulate operation of the treatment element based on the detected characteristic difference, thereby preferentially removing the stenotic material while substantially preserving the integrity of the stent; and
an energy delivery system operably coupled to the control unit and the treatment element, for providing activation energy to the treatment element.

