A method for compensating for temperature effects on a burden resistor in an electrical measurement circuit, the method comprising:
obtaining a raw voltage measurement across the burden resistor;
obtaining a temperature measurement associated with the burden resistor;
accessing stored temperature-resistance characteristic data for the burden resistor, the stored data defining a relationship between the resistance of the burden resistor and temperature;
calculating a temperature-compensated resistance value for the burden resistor based on the obtained temperature measurement and the accessed temperature-resistance characteristic data;
determining a compensated current value flowing through the burden resistor using the obtained raw voltage measurement and the calculated temperature-compensated resistance value; and
outputting the compensated current value.

A method for pseudowire protection, comprising:
establishing an active pseudowire between a first provider edge (PE) device and a second PE device;
establishing a standby pseudowire between the first PE device and the second PE device, wherein the standby pseudowire is configured to carry service traffic upon failure of the active pseudowire;
transmitting the service traffic over the active pseudowire;
monitoring a status of the active pseudowire;
detecting a fault associated with the active pseudowire based on the monitoring; and
in response to detecting the fault, switching transmission of the service traffic from the active pseudowire to the standby pseudowire.

An oscillator, comprising:
