A method for calibrating a downlink transmit path of a base station, the method comprising:
generating a test signal at a baseband processor of the base station;
transmitting the test signal through a downlink transmit chain of the base station;
coupling a portion of the transmitted test signal from the downlink transmit chain to a receive chain within the base station;
down-converting and digitizing the coupled portion of the transmitted test signal to generate a digitized feedback signal;
determining, based on the digitized feedback signal, one or more performance characteristics of the downlink transmit path;
comparing the one or more determined performance characteristics to one or more desired performance characteristics;
calculating one or more calibration parameters for the downlink transmit path based on the comparison; and
applying the one or more calculated calibration parameters to adjust operation of the downlink transmit path during subsequent downlink transmissions.

