A system for registration of a network access device during loss of power, the system comprising:
a network access device, comprising a communication interface configured to transmit and receive data over a network; a power management module configured to monitor an operational power supply of the network access device; a backup power source selectively activatable to provide power to at least a portion of the network access device; and a processor coupled to the communication interface, the power management module, and the backup power source; wherein the processor is configured to:
detect a degradation in the operational power supply via the power management module, indicative of an impending power loss condition;
responsive to detecting the degradation in the operational power supply, activate the backup power source;
initiate a registration procedure with a network server over the network via the communication interface, said registration procedure configured to update a registration state of the network access device with the network server; and
transmit, using power from the activated backup power source, registration data associated with the registration procedure to the network server prior to a complete cessation of the operational power supply, thereby registering the network access device during loss of power.

A system for archival management of database logs, the system comprising:
