A method for tunneling data link layer frames to enable high-speed data transmission in a noisy wireless environment, the method comprising:
  receiving, at a transmitting node, a data link layer frame;
  encapsulating the received data link layer frame into a tunnel frame by adding a tunnel header, the tunnel header comprising error control information and sequencing information;
  applying an adaptive error resilience scheme to the tunnel frame prior to transmission, the adaptive error resilience scheme dynamically adjusting at least one parameter based on sensed wireless channel conditions to mitigate noise effects;
  transmitting the tunnel frame over a wireless medium at a data rate configured for high-speed throughput;
  receiving, at a receiving node, the tunnel frame from the wireless medium;
  processing the received tunnel frame, including performing error detection and, if necessary, error correction or requesting retransmission based on the error control information, the sequencing information, and the adaptive error resilience scheme; and
  decapsulating the original data link layer frame from the processed tunnel frame;
  wherein the encapsulation, adaptive error resilience scheme, and transmission cooperate to maintain high data throughput across the noisy wireless environment.

