a processing chamber;
a substrate support positioned within the processing chamber, adapted to hold a substrate;
one or more precursor delivery systems connected to the processing chamber, adapted to supply one or more film-forming precursors therein;
an energy source connected to the processing chamber, adapted to activate the one or more film-forming precursors to enable deposition of the high dielectric film on the substrate;
a vacuum system connected to the processing chamber, arranged to evacuate said processing chamber; and
a controller operatively coupled to the one or more precursor delivery systems, the energy source, and the vacuum system, adapted to regulate the film formation process to form the high dielectric film on the substrate.

A system for active database event management, the system comprising:
a database adapted to store data and issue one or more trigger events responsive to predefined database operations;
a trigger gateway including one or more processors and memory, the trigger gateway operatively linked to the database;
wherein the trigger gateway is configured to:
obtain the one or more trigger events issued by the database;
determine dynamically, using a set of externally defined trigger configuration rules, one or more trigger actions associated with an obtained trigger event; and
perform the identified one or more trigger actions outside of the database, thus offering a decoupled processing mechanism for database event triggers without integrating trigger logic directly into a database schema.

A rolling bearing comprising:
an inner ring;
an outer ring disposed concentrically with the inner ring;
a plurality of rolling elements positioned between the inner ring and the outer ring;
an integrated generator arranged to generate electrical energy from relative rotational movement between at least two components of the rolling bearing, the integrated generator comprising:
a plurality of magnets secured to a first component chosen from the inner ring, the outer ring, and a cage; and
a plurality of coils secured to a second component chosen from the inner ring, the outer ring, and the cage, said second component being distinct from the first component, such that relative rotation between the first component and the second component induces current in the coils;
a power management circuit electrically connected to the integrated generator, the power management circuit arranged to condition the generated electrical energy;
an energy storage unit electrically connected to the power management circuit for storing conditioned electrical energy; and
an output interface electrically connected to the power management circuit for supplying electrical energy to an external load, wherein said output interface is controlled by a control unit arranged to manage charging of the energy storage unit and discharge of electrical energy.

A method for forming a planarized layer of a semiconductor device, comprising:
providing a semiconductor substrate comprising topographical features, said features defining a non-planar upper surface;
depositing a material layer over the non-planar upper surface of the substrate;
subjecting the deposited material layer to a planarization process, thereby removing portions of the material layer until a substantially planar upper surface is achieved.

1. A three-dimensional clinostat for cultivating cells, comprising:
    a sample holder designed to securely accommodate at least one cell culture vessel;
    a first rotation mechanism coupled to the sample holder, said first rotation mechanism configured to rotate the sample holder around a first axis;
    a second rotation mechanism coupled to the first rotation mechanism, said second rotation mechanism configured to rotate both the first rotation mechanism and the sample holder about a second axis substantially orthogonal to the first axis;
    at least one motor arranged to drive the first rotation mechanism and the second rotation mechanism;
    and a control unit coupled to the at least one motor, wherein the control unit is configured to independently regulate the rotational speed and direction of the first rotation mechanism and the second rotation mechanism to generate a three-dimensional random or quasi-random gravity vector averaging environment for the at least one cell culture vessel.

An apparatus and method for tuning a band pass filter, comprising:
a band pass filter arranged to filter an input signal within a specified frequency range;
a tuning circuit connected to the band pass filter, the tuning circuit adapted to adjust one or more characteristics of the band pass filter, including a center frequency, a bandwidth, and a quality factor;
a control unit connected to the tuning circuit, the control unit operative to generate a control signal for the tuning circuit;
wherein the control unit is further adapted to ascertain a desired characteristic for the band pass filter and to generate the control signal in accordance with the desired characteristic;
and wherein the tuning circuit is further operative to adjust said one or more characteristics of the band pass filter responsive to the control signal.

A conveyance control system, comprising:
multiple sensors adapted to obtain operational data pertaining to a conveyance and environmental data related to the conveyance's surroundings;
a processing unit electronically coupled to the multiple sensors, the processing unit arranged to receive the operational data and the environmental data, to analyze said received data according to a predetermined control logic, and to produce one or more control commands for the conveyance;
an actuation interface linked to the processing unit, the actuation interface adapted to transmit the one or more control commands to one or more conveyance actuators to alter an operational state of the conveyance, said operational state comprising at least one of a speed, a direction, an acceleration, or a position of the conveyance;
a communication interface electronically linked to the processing unit, the communication interface arranged to receive external control inputs pertaining to the conveyance and to transmit conveyance operational status data to an external system; and
a memory unit coupled to the processing unit, the memory unit storing instructions executable by the processing unit to execute the predetermined control logic and retaining operational parameters for controlling the conveyance.

1. An apparatus for processing seismic data, comprising:
    an input module configured to obtain seismic data;
    a processor coupled to the input module and configured to carry out programmed instructions to:
        examine attributes of the obtained seismic data;
        ascertain one or more processing parameters derived from the examined attributes;
        apply said one or more processing parameters to the obtained seismic data to yield processed seismic data, where said processed seismic data presents augmented characteristics for subsurface geological interpretation; and
    an output module coupled to the processor and configured to provide the processed seismic data.

A communication system comprising:
a mobile station adapted to communicate with a network infrastructure;
a network component arranged to manage operational states of the mobile station;
wherein the network component is configured to ascertain a switching instruction for the mobile station based on at least one operational parameter of the mobile station or the network infrastructure;
and wherein the mobile station is configured to receive said switching instruction and, in response, execute a state transition consistent with the switching instruction.

1. A downhole anti-rotation tool comprising:
a tubular body possessing a first end and a second end, the tubular body adapted for coupling with a wellbore tubular string;
at least one radially outwardly extendable anchoring member mounted on the tubular body;
an actuation mechanism operatively connected to the at least one anchoring member, the actuation mechanism arranged to selectively deploy the at least one anchoring member from a retracted state to an extended state;
wherein, in its extended state, the at least one anchoring member is adapted to contact an interior surface of a wellbore; and
whereby engagement of the at least one anchoring member with the interior surface of the wellbore restricts rotation of the tubular body with respect to the wellbore.

An electric motor system for a dental handpiece, comprising:
a handpiece housing adapted for grasping by a user;
an electric motor housed within the handpiece housing;
a drive shaft rotationally linked to the electric motor, the drive shaft extending toward a distal end of the handpiece housing;
a tool coupling mechanism situated at the distal end of the handpiece housing, said mechanism adapted to detachably secure a dental tool to the drive shaft; and
an electrical connector arranged to provide power to the electric motor.

A method for processing a vocal signal using accompaniment music, comprising:
acquiring a vocal input audio signal;
obtaining an accompaniment music input audio signal;
processing the vocal input audio signal to modify at least one attribute thereof, where said modification is predicated at least partly on a characteristic of the accompaniment music input audio signal;
and outputting a processed vocal audio signal.

A method for operating a controlled system configured to generate a control output for influencing a process, the method comprising:
receiving an activation command for a control-hold mode;
responsive to the command, commencing the control-hold mode and recording a current control output value of the controlled system;
while in the control-hold mode, sustaining the recorded control output value as the control output for influencing the process, thereby preserving the process at a state corresponding to the recorded control output value, irrespective of subsequent changes in a control input signal; and
ending the control-hold mode upon receipt of a deactivation command or satisfaction of a predefined condition.

A method for producing a hollow structure for a breathing mask, comprising:
providing a polymeric material;
providing a removable core structure;
forming the polymeric material about the removable core structure to define at least one wall of the hollow structure;
solidifying the polymeric material to form the hollow structure;
extracting the removable core structure from within the solidified polymeric material to define an internal cavity within the hollow structure; and
preparing the hollow structure for use as a component of a breathing mask.

A system comprising:
